                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is the difference between VMS and procurement software?</h3>
                                        <p>VMS is one component of procurement software. Full procurement suites include sourcing / RFP, contract management, VMS, purchasing, invoice processing, and analytics.</p>
                                        <h3>How much does VMS cost?</h3>
                                        <p>Off-shelf India: ₹5-30 lakh/year. Enterprise global (Coupa, Ariba): $50K-500K+/year. Custom builds: ₹40 lakh - 2 Cr.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I use Ariba / Coupa or build custom?</h3>
                                        <p>Ariba / Coupa if you have 200+ vendors, mature procurement processes, and enterprise IT team. Custom if you have industry-specific needs or mid-scale operations.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest VMS mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Weak vendor master data. Duplicate vendors, inconsistent tax IDs, missing PAN / VAT numbers destroy all downstream analytics. Fix vendor master first.</p>
